1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,990
Power Play versus Flex Play comes down to
one basic tradeoff.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,630
A PrizePicks Power Play requires every
active pick to be correct

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,440
for its listed standard payout.

4
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:14,410
A Flex Play has a lower top multiplier at
the same

5
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:17,670
pick count, but it can still return money
when one or

6
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:18,860
two picks are incorrect.

7
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:23,390
That describes the structure, not which
option anyone should choose.

8
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,890
PrizePicks calls these Player Pick
lineups.

9
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,870
Its current help page says a lineup
normally contains two to

10
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:34,640
six projections, with athletes from at
least two different teams.

11
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:36,640
Some limits are regional.

12
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,520
Colorado, for example, requires at least
three projections,

13
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:46,110
and access, age requirements, eligible
sports, and other rules vary by

14
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:50,460
location. As of August sixteenth, twenty
twenty-six,

15
00:00:50,470 --> 00:00:53,550
PrizePicks lists these standard Power Play
payouts:

16
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:56,580
three times the entry for two correct
picks,

17
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:59,860
six times for three, ten times for four,

18
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:04,220
twenty times for five, and thirty-seven
point five times for six.

19
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:07,660
Power is all correct at the active pick
count.

20
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:12,910
Flex uses tiers. The current standard
chart includes two-pick Flex at

21
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:16,210
two times for two correct, or point five
times for one

22
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:19,820
correct. Three-pick Flex pays three times
for three correct,

23
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,290
or one times for two.

24
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:24,680
Four-pick Flex pays six times for four
correct,

25
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:26,970
or one point five times for three.

26
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:31,440
Five-pick and six-pick Flex add a third
partial-result tier.

27
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,680
The complete chart is on screen.

28
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:38,200
Here is a clean four-pick example using a
twenty-dollar entry.

29
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:42,390
At the published standard rate, a
four-pick Power Play returns two

30
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,680
hundred dollars if all four picks are
correct.

31
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:48,230
If one active pick is wrong, it does not
earn that

32
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:52,590
listed Power payout. A four-pick Flex
returns one hundred twenty dollars

33
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,900
for four correct, or thirty dollars for
three correct.

34
00:01:56,560 --> 00:02:00,830
Those are total payouts, not profit, and
this comparison is not

35
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:05,050
an expected-value claim. Now the most
important limitation.

36
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:09,550
PrizePicks says the payout on the
individual details screen is disclosed

37
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:12,980
before submission and can differ from the
standard chart.

38
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:18,020
Projection type, promotions, same-game or
same-team combinations,

39
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:23,570
combined Player and Team Picks, fees, and
other pre-established factors can

40
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:25,100
change the displayed amount.

41
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:29,760
Always treat that current details screen
as the controlling number.

42
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:35,120
DNPs, eligible Reboots, and ties can also
change the outcome.

43
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:40,330
A DNP or eligible Reboot normally removes
that projection and reverts

44
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:41,710
the lineup down one tier.

45
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:45,000
A four-pick Power becomes a three-pick
Power;

46
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:47,840
a four-pick Flex becomes a three-pick
Flex.

47
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:51,920
A two-pick lineup that reverts is normally
refunded,

48
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:56,250
and a reverted lineup can become
ineligible if every remaining athlete

49
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:57,700
is from the same team.

50
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,100
A tie also lowers the payout tier,

51
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:04,930
but the tied projection is not removed for
the minimum-pick or

52
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:09,060
same-team rules. Sport-specific conditions
still apply.

53
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:14,350
Propeller's PrizePicks payout calculator
is useful for illustrating the published

54
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:19,190
standard-rate math. Choose Power or Flex,
select a pick count and

55
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:20,860
entry amount, then calculate.

56
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:25,860
Its optional hit-rate field uses only the
percentage the visitor supplies.

57
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:30,380
That output is a mathematical scenario,
not a prediction,

58
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:35,240
probability claim, recommendation, or
promise about a real lineup.

59
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:38,020
So the short answer is simple.

60
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:42,860
Power concentrates the listed payout on
getting every active pick correct.

61
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:47,770
Flex exchanges some of the top standard
multiplier for additional payout

62
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:51,860
tiers. Neither label tells you whether an
entry is good,

63
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:56,040
and the general chart never overrides the
current details screen.

64
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:58,980
Rules and availability change.

